## 3. Course creation workflow

When the administrator clicks Create Course, open a guided builder with a clear progress indicator, autosave, draft status and a final publishing step.

Step 1 — Basic information

Course name, URL slug, summary, full description, cover image, category, instructor, level, language and learning outcomes.

Step 2 — Curriculum

Add modules and lessons, reorder them, and set each lesson's content type and access level.

Step 3 — Content

Build lessons using video, formatted text, code blocks, downloadable files, quizzes and assignments.

Step 4 — Access and pricing

Choose a free course, a paid course, or free preview lessons with premium content.

Step 5 — Student experience

Configure completion requirements, prerequisites, certificates and optional scheduled content.

Step 6 — Review and publish

Check the course, preview the student view, resolve validation errors and publish.

Important behavior: saving a draft must not publish it automatically. Publishing should validate required information, curriculum integrity, content availability and pricing configuration.

